messages:
charlie_se: Hey team — hitting a 400 from /v1/rerank with a batched payload. Minimal repro below, response included. Anyone seen this?

charlie_se: curl -X POST https://api.redwood.inference/rerank \
  -H 'Authorization: Bearer REDACTED' \
  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
  -d '
{
  "requests": [
    {
      "id": "r1",
      "query": "Which product should I buy?",
      "candidates": [
        {"id":"c1","text":"Prod A"},
        {"id":"c2","text":"Prod B"}
      ]
    }
  ],
  "top_k": "3"
}
'

charlie_se: HTTP/1.1 400 Bad Request
{
  "error": "invalid_request",
  "message": "request validation failed: missing required 'items' array"
}

alice_support: Thanks — can you paste the full response headers / x-request-id? Also are you using our official SDK or a hand-crafted request?

charlie_se: Using our backend service (node) calling curl-style. x-request-id: rq_0b8f9c2a. Payload above is verbatim. We experimented with top_k because our old client used snake_case.

bob_engineer: I can repro locally. Router validation expects topk as a number (topk) and the main array key to be items. When it sees an envelope key of "requests" it attempts a compatibility shim but that path assumes topk is numeric. Sending top_k as a string hits a strict JSON schema check and returns 400.

bob_engineer: Quick notes:
- Wrong envelope key: "requests" instead of "items".
- top_k provided as string "3". Server schema uses integer for topk.
- Some SDKs historically accepted snake_case but a recent router config tightened schema.

bob_engineer: Workaround: change payload to use "items" and a numeric topk (or omit topk to use default). Example:
```json
{
  "items": [
    {
      "id": "r1",
      "query": "Which product should I buy?",
      "candidates": [
        {"id":"c1","text":"Prod A"},
        {"id":"c2","text":"Prod B"}
      ]
    }
  ],
  "topk": 3
}
```

triage-bot: RDW-5212 created: "rerank: strict schema rejects snake_case envelope + string top_k causing 400 on wrapped clients". Priority P2, assigned to bob_engineer.

alice_support: Thanks @bob_engineer. @charlie_se — if you can deploy the two-line change (rename key + ensure topk is numeric) it should unblock you immediately. We'll keep RDW-5212 open and push a compatibility patch to allow string numbers for topk in the shim. ETA for patch: next patch window (48h).

charlie_se: Great — thanks. Will patch now and report back. Appreciate the quick triage. :+1:
